 "recommendation": {
  "expected_effects": "Taker cost -15% (spread -15%, no fees added). Depth flat to slightly up (~48.5 vs 48.2). Mispricing flat to slightly down. Volatility flat vs default (no increase). Makers remain profitable, exchange revenue 0 (neutral).",
  "rationale": "A 1% circuit breaker was the only lever to cut all-in investor costs materially (-15%) with zero fees: it disrupts tacit wide quoting (collusion 0.41 to 0.07) and forces tighter spreads. Maker rebates narrowed quotes but raised all-in cost, and speed bumps raised depth but undid spread gains and raised costs. The single-lever breaker keeps books, mispricing, volatility and profitability in line with defaults, so it should generalize out of sample.",
  "rules": {
   "circuit_breaker_pct": 1.0
  }
 },
